From: Abhishek <abhishek01789@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 17:43:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/40] Rebuild the drag effect as KDE-style wobbly windows

A 4x4 grid of springs bends the window around the grabbed point. Only
15% of the window's motion becomes bend (KDE's move factor) and every
point is always pulled home, so it wobbles instead of trailing like
jelly. The window fades to 80% while dragged, like KDE's Translucency.
---
 packages/config/src/effect/jelly-drag.frag |  55 +++-
 packages/config/src/jelly-drag.ts          | 309 ++++++++++++++-------
 2 files changed, 246 insertions(+), 118 deletions(-)

